        "worked_solution": "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $Q$ is $p=⟨-1,0,4⟩$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-4,1⟩$  and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1,0,4⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨0,-1,\\sqrt{3}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
